 {'id':'frontier','title':'Security frontier · Shared defense, passkeys and policies','steps':['Open Security frontier in the sidebar. Explicitly enable shared synthetic defense in two test accounts; a high-risk denial of an unchanged Judge Demo Pack fixture can add fixed attack categories to the public feed. Matching opted-in proposals stop before model processing. Personal documents never enroll.','Register a passkey on the exact deployed HTTPS origin. Create a hold for a pending synthetic invoice, then release with your authenticator. User verification may use a PIN or biometric; all ordinary checks still apply. No real funds, HSM attestation or banking connection is involved.','Request a live Meta policy proposal, inspect its 1,024 deterministic fixture results, then explicitly promote or roll back. Policies can only add denials or lower the amount ceiling; no model can rewrite executable guardrails or approve payments. Fixture results are not real-world accuracy or mathematical proof.']},
